{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Dream With Me feels like a natural next choice because its classical crossover sound connects with the sweeping vocals I sought in A Musical Affair and Stages.",
    "I Dreamed A Dream fits my interest in expressive ballads and musical theatre, while the Christmas selections recognize a seasonal interest I have explored before."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "World From the Side of the Moon and Red feel less suited to the calm, orchestral vocal listening I want now, even though I have explored other popular vocal albums.",
    "The holiday albums match a past interest but not my present mood, and Something Beautiful gives me too little evidence of the sound I am seeking."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in 747 and Golden seems to have been taken as a broader desire for country and pop vocals than I feel right now.",
    "My previous Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing preference regardless of whether I currently want seasonal music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interaction with relaxing classical music matters because I currently want a calmer listen, alongside the expressive vocals found in several earlier choices.",
    "The strongest connection for me is the combination of orchestral accompaniment, sweeping vocals, and musical theatre material; simply featuring a singer is not enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The selections recognize my interest in expressive singing but give too little weight to my current preference for calm classical crossover and orchestral vocals."
}"}
